 "text": "Bourbon County Kansas – The official website of Bourbon County, Kansas\nTEL 620-223-3800\nHome\nSheriff’s Office\nHome\nSheriff’s Office\nFollow\nFollow\nAbout\nHistory\nMedia Releases\nMaps\nLinks\nDepartments\nMinutes\nArchives\n2019 Minutes\n2018 Minutes\n2017 Minutes\n2016 Minutes\n2015 Minutes\nElected Officials\nCity Governments\nFinance\nBudgets\nRegister of Deeds\nCounty Clerk\nElection\nAppraiser\nGIS\nTreasurer\nPublic Works\nHuman Resources\nJob Openings\nEmployees\nEmployee Email\nEmployee Resources\nInformation Technology\nPublic Safety\nGet Emergency Alerts\nSheriff’s Office\nPublic Health\nEmergency Management\nReport Road Problem\nSanitation\nResidents\nFair Housing Contacts\nGenealogy\nOpen Records\nSales Tax Rates\nVehicle Registration\nTax Sale\nRecords Information\nTax Search\nParcel Search\nDistrict Court Search\nRMIS On-Line Search\nCommunity Links\nFS Area Chamber\nCity of Fort Scott\nCity of Uniontown\nFSCC\nUSD 234 – Fort Scott\nUSD 235 – Uniontown\nAbout\nHistory\nMedia Releases\nMaps\nLinks\nDepartments\nMinutes\nArchives\n2019 Minutes\n2018 Minutes\n2017 Minutes\n2016 Minutes\n2015 Minutes\nElected Officials\nCity Governments\nFinance\nBudgets\nRegister of Deeds\nCounty Clerk\nElection\nAppraiser\nGIS\nTreasurer\nPublic Works\nHuman Resources\nJob Openings\nEmployees\nEmployee Email\nEmployee Resources\nInformation Technology\nPublic Safety\nGet Emergency Alerts\nSheriff’s Office\nPublic Health\nEmergency Management\nReport Road Problem\nSanitation\nResidents\nFair Housing Contacts\nGenealogy\nOpen Records\nSales Tax Rates\nVehicle Registration\nTax Sale\nRecords Information\nTax Search\nParcel Search\nDistrict Court Search\nRMIS On-Line Search\nCommunity Links\nFS Area Chamber\nCity of Fort Scott\nCity of Uniontown\nFSCC\nUSD 234 – Fort Scott\nUSD 235 – Uniontown\nWelcome to Bourbon County\nBourbon County, Kansas, was one of the thirty-three original counties of Kansas created by the first Territorial Assembly of 1855. The area containing the present Bourbon County was part of the Louisiana Purchase of 1803 .\nBourbon County is full of rich history, dating back to the Civil War. Our county seat, Fort Scott, is home to the 1842 Fort Scott National Historic Site, as well as National Cemetery No. 1, and beautiful mansions.\nLearn More\nInformation Center\nCounty Clerk Documents\nKansas Fishing\nNews and Announcements\nCommission Minutes 08.03.26\nAug 14, 2026\nCommission Minutes 08.03.26\nread more\nCommission Minutes 07.27.26\nAug 14, 2026\nCommission Minutes 07.27.26\nread more\nCommission Minutes 07.20.26\nJul 29, 2026\nCommission Minutes 07.20.26\nread more\nCommission Minutes 07.22.26\nJul 29, 2026\nCommission Special Meeting 07.22.26\nread more\nQuick Links\n\nJob Openings\n\nMedia Releases\n\nReport Road problem\n\nHours of Operation\n\nElected Officials\n\nSheriff's Office\nLocation\nBourbon County\n210 S. National Ave.\nFort Scott, Kansas 66701\nCourthouse hours\n​ Monday – Friday\n8:30AM – 4:30PM\nTELEPHONE\n620-223-3800\nStaff eMail\nHome\nSheriff’s Office\nHome\nSheriff’s Office\nCopyright © Bourbon County, Kansas | All rights reserved\nRedlogic Communications, Inc.",
